(Let's outline:)
(- Origin: already has link and prepared.)
(- We'll assign operator to origin, lock origin, release operator.)
(- Assemble leg (needs origin lock and destination lock, etc.))
(- Authorize loading (needs origin lock and candidate_task_profile_linked origin).)
(- Mark origin dispatch ready (needs origin lock, origin confirmed, leg assembled, loading authorized). At this point we still have link.)
(- After marking origin dispatch ready, we can detach task profile from origin (detach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha). This will make route_task_profile_available true.)
(- Then attach task profile to shift_candidate_beta.)
(- Then confirm candidate_prepared for shift_candidate_beta (requires vehicle_allocated and candidate_task_profile_linked). We'll have vehicle allocated earlier (step8). So after attaching profile, we can confirm prepared.)
(- Then assign operator, skill certificate, compliance certificate (after releasing from alpha).)
(- Then load container onto leg (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, etc.))
(- Then stage schedule candidate (requires candidate_prepared, loading container linked, loaded, leg linked, task profile linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading))
(- Then verify loading profile nominal.)
(- Then establish clearance nominal.)
(- Then attach service window.)
(- Then validate route sequence (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, candidate_service_window_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_destination_availability_linked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, candidate_task_profile_linked, not route_sequence_validated). Note: candidate_origin_availability_linked and candidate_destination_availability_linked are already true (init). Good.)
(- Then finalize candidate after sequence validation.)
(- Then allocate dispatch slot for shift_candidate_beta.)
(- Then execute dispatch shift_candidate_beta.)
